Title: F1-M05 — Paper Wolves (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

FADE IN:

INT. RECONNAISSANCE DARKROOM - NIGHT

[[AMBIENCE: dripping fixer, a ventilation fan, muffled generator]]
[[MUSIC: low, uneasy]]

Aerial photographs are pegged on a wire above a trough. CAPTAIN ELIAN and MIRA stand over them.

MIRA
(analytical)
Aerial photographs show a command post with a wall of guns. The detail is too perfect. It may be a stage set.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(neutral)
Too perfect how?

MIRA
(dry)
Guns with no crews. Tents with no tracks in front of them. A fortress that nobody walks in or out of proves only that somebody wanted us to photograph it.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: forward post in the west, north road to the fort, south road past the sheds, grain exchange in the south-east, guard camp beyond it]]

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(firm)
They want us to spend shells on empty ground. Find the supply office that supports the display.

MIRA
(measured)
Use the captured markings if you can. Confirm the real target, then strike it.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(short)
Two of their tanks, still in their paint. The pickets will wave them through until somebody fires. After that the paint is worthless.

MIRA
(concerned)
We have two thousand credits and a strike force, no reserve. Spend it on the fort and there is nothing left for the real target.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(pointing at map)
Decoys of our own along the north road. Let their probes shoot timber.

MIRA
(dry)
And if the fort is timber too, I want to know who sold it to them. Somebody wrote an invoice for all that canvas.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

FADE OUT.
